DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The "status" property of the device tree node indicates whether the de‐
     vice is enabled or not.  Multiple hardware versions might be built using
     the same base System-on-Chip but with a different set of blocks enabled.
     It is common to use  SoC device tree and only enable/disable device nodes
     for the derivative boards.  The device tree node is considered enabled
     only if it has "status" property with the value set to either "ok" or
     "okay".

     ooffww__bbuuss__ggeett__ssttaattuuss() returns the value of the "status" property of the
     device tree node associated with the device _d_e_v.  If the node does not
     have "status" property or there is no node associated with the device the
     function returns NULL.

     ooffww__bbuuss__ssttaattuuss__ookkaayy() returns 1 if the device tree node associated with
     the device _d_e_v has "status" property and its value is either "ok" or
     "okay".

     ooffww__bbuuss__nnooddee__ssttaattuuss__ookkaayy() returns 1 if the device tree node _n_o_d_e has
     "status" property and its value is either "ok" or "okay".

